{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1173323-war-of-the-matriarchs-actual-play","id":1173323,"title":"War of the Matriarchs (actual play)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-04T14:11:46-08:00","id":1173323,"title":"War of the Matriarchs (actual play)","content":"Premise. In a large town two vampire families have come near to all out war, an enterprising Dragon nomad has Mass Enbraced herself a brood in the hopes that they will be able (as good little Mekhets) to escalate things to the point where both sides weaken the other and they can take over.<br /> The cast. Micky an ex ghoul to a now dead Daeva, talky first, thinky second with just enough physical skills to flee a fight.<br /> Apex the hacker and conspiracy nut who found more than expected and was lucky about who noticed him as he did, skilled in computer and investigation related stuff and able to get out of a bad situation when needed.<br /> Sam the fire person who has an axe and knows how to use it, an empathic (hurt locker merit) individual who knows how fire starts, the reason they were picked for embrace should be obvious.<br /> Jim the bar tender and small time crook, knows how to talk to people.<br /> Bran the ex cop who to be honest assumed the group would need someone who could fight and worked out from there, very much a &quot;bad cop&quot; type of guy.<br /> The embrace. Their sire Heather performs the scale and feeds the chained up fledglings rats until they calm down then releases them and talks them though what's happening to them, they socialise.<br /> Highlights include Sam asking Jim what he does, Jim saying he is sort of the opposite to Bran to which Bran responds &quot;so you create unnecessary paperwork&quot; and Jim seeing which of the team would spot his attempts to pick their pockets.<br /> With session zero out of the way we began our first real session with Mumpire having to leave town for a bit and wishing them luck, then everyone rolled to see how much Vitae they had, most of the group needed to feed so ahunting they did go. Jim feeds fine. Bran fails, breaks into a house and feeds from the sleeping occupant, frenzies with a dramatic fail, kills him but passes his detachment roll so I cut to the next guy while deciding what to do with a dramatic failure. Apex jumps a guy in an alley, avoids frenzy, decided no witnesses and failed his detachment roll, checked the options for his Mekhet bane and wrote Rat Pimp on his sheet before joining the others at the bar.<br /> Cutting back to Bran who had wandered into Gangrel turf with the competitive condition before the Beast gave him back his body he turns and heads home not noticing the gang of vampires who block his path and retreat in an alley, first he tries to bluff/intimidate them that he's one of the Daeva before pushing past them and running, one of them catches up and gets a broken baseball bat through the chest for his trouble, Bran is gone before the rest arrive.<br /> Back at the bar the gang wait for him (he called to let them know what happened) and when he arrives he explains about the dead guy he needs to sort out.<br /> Cops had taken the body to the morgue by the time they get there so Sam, Apex and Bran go to the morgue (Bran rolls well enough to know it from his time as a cop) bluff past a apathetic night watchman who didn't know Bran had been kicked off the force, luck out and find the dead body room empty, someone finds the password on a postit note and they mark the body for incineration in the morning before walking briskly for the exit.<br /> Next session they plan to spark the war via driving a petrol tanker into a Gangrel haven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T03:59:25-08:00","id":1173465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1173323-war-of-the-matriarchs-actual-play#post1173323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Premise. In a large town two vampire families have come near to all out war, an enterprising Dragon nomad has Mass Enbraced herself a brood in the hopes that they will be able (as good little Mekhets) to escalate things to the point where both sides weaken the other and they can take over.<br /> The cast. Micky an ex ghoul to a now dead Daeva, talky first, thinky second with just enough physical skills to flee a fight.<br /> Apex the hacker and conspiracy nut who found more than expected and was lucky about who noticed him as he did, skilled in computer and investigation related stuff and able to get out of a bad situation when needed.<br /> Sam the fire person who has an axe and knows how to use it, an empathic (hurt locker merit) individual who knows how fire starts, the reason they were picked for embrace should be obvious.<br /> Jim the bar tender and small time crook, knows how to talk to people.<br /> Bran the ex cop who to be honest assumed the group would need someone who could fight and worked out from there, very much a &quot;bad cop&quot; type of guy.<br /> The embrace. Their sire Heather performs the scale and feeds the chained up fledglings rats until they calm down then releases them and talks them though what's happening to them, they socialise.<br /> Highlights include Sam asking Jim what he does, Jim saying he is sort of the opposite to Bran to which Bran responds &quot;so you create unnecessary paperwork&quot; and Jim seeing which of the team would spot his attempts to pick their pockets.<br /> With session zero out of the way we began our first real session with Mumpire having to leave town for a bit and wishing them luck, then everyone rolled to see how much Vitae they had, most of the group needed to feed so ahunting they did go. Jim feeds fine. Bran fails, breaks into a house and feeds from the sleeping occupant, frenzies with a dramatic fail, kills him but passes his detachment roll so I cut to the next guy while deciding what to do with a dramatic failure. Apex jumps a guy in an alley, avoids frenzy, decided no witnesses and failed his detachment roll, checked the options for his Mekhet bane and wrote Rat Pimp on his sheet before joining the others at the bar.<br /> Cutting back to Bran who had wandered into Gangrel turf with the competitive condition before the Beast gave him back his body he turns and heads home not noticing the gang of vampires who block his path and retreat in an alley, first he tries to bluff/intimidate them that he's one of the Daeva before pushing past them and running, one of them catches up and gets a broken baseball bat through the chest for his trouble, Bran is gone before the rest arrive.<br /> Back at the bar the gang wait for him (he called to let them know what happened) and when he arrives he explains about the dead guy he needs to sort out.<br /> Cops had taken the body to the morgue by the time they get there so Sam, Apex and Bran go to the morgue (Bran rolls well enough to know it from his time as a cop) bluff past a apathetic night watchman who didn't know Bran had been kicked off the force, luck out and find the dead body room empty, someone finds the password on a postit note and they mark the body for incineration in the morning before walking briskly for the exit.<br /> Next session they plan to spark the war via driving a petrol tanker into a Gangrel haven.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really wonder how this driving a petrol tanker into a haven will turn out. Because unless the haven is really ,really isolated then I could definietly see the humans starting to seriously investigate and potentially label it as a terrorist attack and start to dig very deep, as well as put local law enforcemen on high alert if a culprit can't be produced fairly quick. Could even get the Feds into town.<br /> <br /> Granted I'm not an American but this is would I would suspect to be the outcome from an overt action like that.<br /> <br /> Still sounds like something that will shake things up in this town! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T04:27:23-08:00","id":1173468,"title":"","content":"I had no thinking needed during the whole session, the dice dictated they must feed, the dice dictated the man needed to die, the dramatic failure and us agreeing that competitive made most sense meant Bran ended up in enemy territory. The game ran itself.<br /> And honestly this is known by the players to be a suicide campaign, they could win but the deck is so stacked against them that I wouldn't be surprised if they're dead by session 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T04:26:57-08:00","id":1189190,"title":"","content":"Sorry it's been so long but my life has been hectic, the petrol tanker plan went very well all things considered. First Micky agreed to acquire balaclavas on the understanding that he be excused from further involvement in this disaster and Jim asked what time they were expecting a delivery claiming to need to know when the staition would be unable to operate (the player had worked in a petrol staition and said that this is a thing that happens) then the group opened a (whatever those big metal things with computer circuits inside are called) and Apex got to work arranging for a red light.<br /> Bran and Sam did the hijacking and drove the tanker towards their target then with the help of a friendly cinder block left the tanker travaling forwards with it's cargo leaking (Bran climbed across the tanker as it was moving to open it's tap/port thing) and the two of them fled, Bran lit the oil and frenzied and Sam got into a brief fight with a cop who fled when his options became save people from a burning building or fight someone using a fire axe.<br /> Bran failed his detachment roll and his police badge no longer serves as a touchstone as he realised that he's no longer serving the public good.<br /> I don't have time before work to do justice to the following game but I promise that Operation Gimp from the Deep is a beautiful example of player logic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}